      "operator": "Helmut Schindlwick + Claude (AI pair-programmer)",
      "source_note": "Hand-curated from published portfolio documentation (retrieved 2026-08-06). Delos Cloud GmbH (100 percent SAP subsidiary, Walldorf), Microsoft technology, Arvato Systems operations with security-vetted German staff; datacentres in Berlin and Frankfurt am Main with a second operations centre near Leipzig (live early 2026). EU-entity operator: Delos Cloud GmbH and Arvato Systems are German/EU entities -- CLOUD Act does not attach via ownership or operations. Residual risk: Microsoft (US jurisdiction) remains the technology licensor and software supplier; this is a supply-chain dependency, not a legal extraterritorial attachment, and is recorded here for framework evaluation. A November 2025 code-access MoU between SAP, Arvato, and Microsoft mitigates the update-dependency concern (sap.com 2025-11-18). certifications: [] is deliberate -- no Delos-specific BSI C5 Testat or IT-Grundschutz certificate is published (verified absence 2026-08-06); the BSI oversight design intent and VS-NfD roadmap are noted so the field can be populated the day a Testat appears. No BYOK/HYOK/Customer Key/Managed HSM documentation exists publicly (verified absence 2026-08-06) -- a material finding for sovereignty assessments demanding customer key custody. key_custody: ['provider-managed'] baseline; Azure Key Vault with CMK is the strongest documented option. confidence: low -- portfolio statuses are published as planned, per-service GA dates are unverified (the roadmap page blocks automated retrieval), and commercial GA date is unconfirmed. Pricing: approximately 10-20 percent above Microsoft list prices (reported, unverified per-service). Status policy: portfolio entries are announced by default; the Azure Foundational tier (core compute/storage/network exercised in pilots) is preview; nothing is ga until confirmable. Sources: deloscloud.de/products/portfolio.html; news.microsoft.com/de-de 2024-09-23; news.sap.com/germany 2024-09; arvato-systems.com; adesso.de; computerwoche.de 2024-11; openai.com/global-affairs/openai-for-germany/ 2025-09; sap.com/germany/documents/2025/11 (code-access MoU); netzpolitik.org/2024 (sovereignty debate context)."
    },
    "confidence": "low",
    "regions_count": 1
  },
